{"name":"Edgewater","hex":"#c1d8c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Edgewater","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A suburb of Perth in the City of Joondalup, Western Australia.","A community in the Regional District of East Kootenay, British Columbia, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Edgewater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Edgewater, Western Australia","blocks":[{"text":"Edgewater is a suburb of Perth, Western Australia 23 kilometres (14 mi) north of Perth's central business district. Edgewater was approved as a suburb name in 1974, and its local government area is the City of Joondalup. It is named after its location on the western edge of Lake Joondalup, which is surrounded by Yellagonga Regional Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/WTJ_Toos42_Edgewater_platform.jpg/330px-WTJ_Toos42_Edgewater_platform.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edgewater%2C_Western_Australia","wikidata":"Q5337833"},{"title":"Edgewater, Alabama","blocks":[{"text":"Edgewater is a census-designated place in Jefferson County, Alabama, United States. It is northeast from the Birmingham suburb of Pleasant Grove. As of the 2020 census, Edgewater had a population of 746. This area was damaged by tornadoes on April 15, 1956 and April 8, 1998. The 1998 tornado was rated F5 on the Fujita scale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Jefferson_County_Alabama_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Edgewater_Highlighted.svg/330px-Jefferson_County_Alabama_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Edgewater_Highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edgewater%2C_Alabama","wikidata":"Q1018651"},{"title":"Edgewater (Barrytown, New York)","blocks":[{"text":"Edgewater is an architecturally significant, early 19th-century house located near the hamlet of Barrytown in Dutchess County, New York, United States. Built about 1824, the house is a contributing property to the Hudson River Historic District. Edgewater's principal architectural feature is a monumental colonnade of six Doric columns, looking out across a lawn to the Hudson River. Writing in 1942, the historians Eberlein and Hubbard described Edgewater as an exemplar of \"the combined dignity and subtle grace that marked the houses of the Federal Era.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/West_Facade_%28Front%29_at_Edgewater_in_Barrytown_New_York_%282018%29.jpg/330px-West_Facade_%28Front%29_at_Edgewater_in_Barrytown_New_York_%282018%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edgewater_(Barrytown%2C_New_York)","wikidata":"Q5337834"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7b/Robert_Donaldson_1820.jpg/330px-Robert_Donaldson_1820.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7b/Robert_Donaldson_1820.jpg/330px-Robert_Donaldson_1820.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Robert Donaldson (portrayed by Charles R. Leslie) and his wife, Susan Gaston Donaldson (portrayed by George Cooke) lived at Edgewater from 1853 until her death in 1866 and his in 1872.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARobert_Donaldson_1820.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Mrs._Robert_Donaldson_%28Susan_Jane_Gaston%29_-_George_Cooke.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Mrs._Robert_Donaldson_%28Susan_Jane_Gaston%29_-_George_Cooke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Mrs._Robert_Donaldson_%28Susan_Jane_Gaston%29_-_George_Cooke.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Mrs._Robert_Donaldson_%28Susan_Jane_Gaston%29_-_George_Cooke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrooklyn_Museum_-_Mrs._Robert_Donaldson_(Susan_Jane_Gaston)_-_George_Cooke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Elizabeth_Winthrop_Chanler.JPG/500px-Elizabeth_Winthrop_Chanler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Elizabeth_Winthrop_Chanler.JPG/1280px-Elizabeth_Winthrop_Chanler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Elizabeth_Winthrop_Chanler.JPG/500px-Elizabeth_Winthrop_Chanler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Elizabeth Chapman (portrayed by John Singer Sargent) bought Edgewater in 1902.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElizabeth_Winthrop_Chanler.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/GoreVidalVanVechten1.jpg/500px-GoreVidalVanVechten1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/GoreVidalVanVechten1.jpg/1280px-GoreVidalVanVechten1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/GoreVidalVanVechten1.jpg/500px-GoreVidalVanVechten1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gore Vidal (photographed by Carl Van Vechten) in 1948, two years before he bought Edgewater.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoreVidalVanVechten1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Edgewater%2C_Station_Road%2C_Barrytown%2C_Dutchess_County%2C_NY_HABS_NY%2C14-BARTO.V%2C1-_%28sheet_2_of_5%29.png/2